("efficiency enhancements") For the months-long residuals (surface classification, Lefschetz, wild-ball complements, Stokes on manifolds), these could help once the quick ones are under way:
- a **Mathlib search** before each blueprint node, since several "missing" pieces turned out to exist in some form;
- **reviewed blueprints**, so formalisation jobs don't stop on representation problems;
- running the **hardest blueprint nodes on a stronger model seat**, at a higher quota cost per job.
